T RankIndex                     | RowSequence.h | 47-97   | owning                        | -  | Counted ordering over the sequence, answering both scroll questions in logarithmic time. power-of-two run ending at its ordinal, so a prefix count and a search by count are both a walk of the set bits of an ordinal rather than of the rows. first and scrolling to a selection needs the second, and a linear answer to either is felt at a thousand rows.
    has   RunCounts    std::vector<std::uint32_t>  [-]  ?
    has   RowCounted   std::vector<bool>           [-]  ?
    has   SpannedRows  std::uint32_t               [-]  ?
    has   CountedRows  std::uint32_t               [-]  ?
    by    Source/OutlinerPanel.cpp, Source/RowSequence.cpp
    note  📐 A binary-indexed count over the row ordering: each stored word carries the visible count of a
    note  🔴 The two questions are not symmetric conveniences. Scrolling to an arbitrary position needs the

